H('CHAPTER 4  IMPLEMENTATION, TESTING AND RESULTS, PROJECT MANAGEMENT')
H('4.1 Development Approach and Resources',2);P('Develop incrementally: fix dialect and corpus; integrate parser and metadata; implement and unit-test rules; connect a least-privilege adapter; add equivalence and plan capture; then benchmark and report. Introduce each rule behind a flag with positive and negative precondition tests.')
table(['Resource','Specification to complete'],[['Language and parser','[Select and record version]'],['Target RDBMS','[Engine, version, configuration]'],['Dataset','[Source, scale, schema, privacy status]'],['Hardware / OS','[CPU, RAM, storage, operating system]'],['Version control / test framework','[Tool and version]']])
H('4.2 System Modules',2);bullets(['SQL front end parses statements and blocks unsupported or non-read-only forms.','Schema catalog resolves metadata needed for rewrite checks.','Optimizer applies guarded rules and records provenance.','DBMS adapter applies parameters and timeouts and captures EXPLAIN output.','Validator compares baseline and candidate results on deterministic test data.','Benchmark reporter repeats measurements and retains raw evidence.'])
H('4.3 Implementation Details',2);P('Predicate pushdown is allowed only when moving a filter across an operator preserves null and outer-join semantics. Projection pruning retains all columns required for output, predicates, grouping, ordering, and later operators. Join reordering is initially restricted to associative and commutative inner joins with compatible predicates. Outer joins and nondeterministic expressions are excluded unless proven safe. Candidates not proven equivalent are not benchmarked as validated wins.')
P('Use an isolated benchmark schema or snapshot, read-only role, statement timeout, fixed parameter values, and documented statistics. Store raw timings, query fingerprints, plans, software versions, and run order; avoid sensitive result content in logs.')
H('4.4 Testing and Evaluation Method',2);P('Correctness tests cover parser behavior, rule preconditions, nulls, duplicates, empty inputs, type coercion, and deterministic result equivalence. Performance tests use the same data snapshot and parameters, a warm-up, at least 10 measured repetitions, controlled or randomized order, and documented concurrency. Report median and P95, plan differences, available resource indicators, and rejected candidates.')
